# The pins every package and every CI job share. One file, three consumers:
#
#   Makefile          include shared/versions.env   → TEST_IMAGE ?= $(DEFAULT_TEST_IMAGE)
#   shell / npm       . shared/versions.sh          → exports the un-prefixed names
#   .github/workflows . shared/versions.env         → $DEFAULT_PI_VERSION
#
# Plain KEY=value, no spaces around `=`, no quotes — that is the intersection of
# what GNU make, POSIX sh and `>> $GITHUB_ENV` all accept. Keep it that way.
#
# Every name is DEFAULT_-prefixed, and every consumer maps DEFAULT_X to X only
# when X is unset. That is what keeps `make check PI_MODEL=...` and a CI job's
# `env:` working: sourcing this file directly would overwrite them, since a
# plain assignment does not care that the variable was already exported.
#
# These were previously duplicated: the image digest in three files, the model in
# five. Each copy carried a comment saying the copies had to move together, which
# is the sound a single source of truth makes before it exists.

# ── The test image ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pinned by digest, not by :latest. The git capability probe asserts what this
# userland's perl-less git can do, and that claim is only worth anything against
# a known image — on a moving tag a base-image change would alter the result
# silently.
#
# It must be the digest of the multi-arch *index* — the one whose manifests[]
# lists both linux/amd64 and linux/arm64. CI runs amd64 and the dev machines are
# arm64, and a per-platform digest satisfies only one of them: `podman pull` by
# digest does not enforce a platform, so the wrong one pulls fine and then dies
# at `podman run` with "Exec format error". `podman inspect --format '{{index
# .RepoDigests 0}}'` reports the per-platform digest on Apple silicon, which is
# exactly how this pin was once broken. Re-pin with the index digest instead:
#   skopeo inspect --raw docker://ghcr.io/ocramz/pi-container-distroless-node24:latest \
#     | skopeo manifest-digest /dev/stdin
# or, with no skopeo, straight from the registry:
#   TOKEN=$(curl -s 'https://ghcr.io/token?scope=repository:ocramz/pi-container-distroless-node24:pull' | jq -r .token)
#   curl -sI -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
#     -H 'Accept: application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json' \
#     https://ghcr.io/v2/ocramz/pi-container-distroless-node24/manifests/latest \
#     | grep -i docker-content-digest
# Then check it with `podman manifest inspect <ref>`: two platforms, not one.
DEFAULT_TEST_IMAGE=ghcr.io/ocramz/pi-container-distroless-node24@sha256:597c258a8b963b975811c98b0a0a32a6faceb4bdd94b1c586e5db4797517512b

# ── The model the live tiers drive ───────────────────────────────────
# The live suites spend money, and the live tier is the only coverage an
# extension's entry point has. deepseek-v4-flash is the cheapest model in the
# catalog that still drives tool calls reliably: the suites need the model to
# actually call a registered tool and the bash tool, and weaker ones narrate
# instead. A concrete id, not the `-latest` alias, so a catalog change cannot
# move it underneath the tests. Override with `make check PI_MODEL=...`.
DEFAULT_PI_PROVIDER=openrouter
DEFAULT_PI_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash

# ── The pi release the packages are written against ──────────────────
# CI installs this globally so the interactive tier drives a known TUI: a release
# that changed it would otherwise turn into a mystery failure. It must stay in
# step with the four @earendil-works/* versions in shared/typecheck/package.json,
# which is what the type-check resolves against. That file has to carry literals
# — a lockfile cannot interpolate — so the pair is kept honest by a comment there
# pointing back here.
DEFAULT_PI_VERSION=0.84.2
